{"surah": 13, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "الٓمٓرۚ تِلْكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِۗ وَٱلَّذِىٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ ٱلْحَقُّ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ ", "translation": "Alif, Lām, Meem, Rā.[1] These are the verses of the Book; and what has been revealed to you from your Lord is the truth, but most of the people do not believe.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "الٓمٓر", "translit": "rٓmٓlā", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِt", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَّبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِى رَفَعَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَاۖ ثُمَّ ٱسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى ٱلْعَرْشِۖ وَسَخَّرَ ٱلشَّمْسَ وَٱلْقَمَرَۖ كُلٌّ يَجْرِى لِأَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىۚ يُدَبِّرُ ٱلْأَمْرَ يُفَصِّلُ ٱلْءَايَٰتِ لَعَلَّكُم بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّكُمْ تُوقِنُونَ ", "translation": "It is Allāh who erected the heavens without pillars that you [can] see; then He established Himself above the Throne[1] and made subject[2] the sun and the moon, each running [its course] for a specified term. He arranges [each] matter; He details the signs that you may, of the meeting with your Lord, be certain.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَفَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَfَr", "root": "رفع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِغَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَغِb", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَمَدٍ", "translit": "ٍdَmَʿع", "root": "عمد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَرَوْنَهَا", "translit": "āَhَnْwَrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱسْتَوَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَwَtْsٱ", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَرْشِ", "translit": "ِhsْrَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عرش"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَسَخَّرَ", "translit": "َrَّhkَsَw", "root": "سخر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلشَّمْسَ", "translit": "َsْmَّhslٱ", "root": "شمس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَٱلْقَمَرَ", "translit": "َrَmَqْlٱَw", "root": "قمر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كُلٌّ", "translit": "ٌّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَجْرِى", "translit": "àِrْjgَy", "root": "جري"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لِأَجَلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَjgَaʾِl", "root": "اجل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مُّسَمًّى", "translit": "àًّmَsُّm", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يُدَبِّرُ", "translit": "ُrِّbَdُy", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرَ", "translit": "َrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يُفَصِّلُ", "translit": "ُlِّṣَfُy", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْءَايَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyāَءْlٱ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "لَعَلَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "بِلِقَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَqِlِb", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "رَبِّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "تُوقِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِqwُt", "root": "يقن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَهُوَ ٱلَّذِى مَدَّ ٱلْأَرْضَ وَجَعَلَ فِيهَا رَوَٰسِىَ وَأَنْهَٰرًاۖ وَمِن كُلِّ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ جَعَلَ فِيهَا زَوْجَيْنِ ٱثْنَيْنِۖ يُغْشِى ٱلَّيْلَ ٱلنَّهَارَۚ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ", "translation": "And it is He who spread the earth and placed therein firmly set mountains and rivers; and from all of the fruits He made therein two mates; He causes the night to cover the day. Indeed in that are signs for a people who give thought.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَدَّ", "translit": "َّdَm", "root": "مدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَجَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَوَٰسِىَ", "translit": "َàِsَٰwَr", "root": "رسو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَنْهَٰرًا", "translit": "āًrَٰhْnَaʾَw", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰrَmَّhtlٱ", "root": "ثمر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "جَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "زَوْجَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَjgْwَz", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱثْنَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَnْhtٱ", "root": "ثني"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يُغْشِى", "translit": "àِhsْغُy", "root": "غشو"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلَّيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَّlٱ", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلنَّهَارَ", "translit": "َrāَhَّnlٱ", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لَءَايَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "لِّقَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَqِّl", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَتَفَكَّرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَّkَfَtَy", "root": "فكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَفِى ٱلْأَرْضِ قِطَعٌ مُّتَجَٰوِرَٰتٌ وَجَنَّٰتٌ مِّنْ أَعْنَٰبٍ وَزَرْعٌ وَنَخِيلٌ صِنْوَانٌ وَغَيْرُ صِنْوَانٍ يُسْقَىٰ بِمَآءٍ وَٰحِدٍ وَنُفَضِّلُ بَعْضَهَا عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ فِى ٱلْأُكُلِۚ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَعْقِلُونَ ", "translation": "And within the land are neighboring plots and gardens of grapevines and crops and palm trees, [growing] several from a root or otherwise,[1] watered with one water; but We make some of them exceed others in [quality of] fruit. Indeed in that are signs for a people who reason.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَفِى", "translit": "àِfَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قِطَعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعَṭِq", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّتَجَٰوِرَٰتٌ", "translit": "ٌtَٰrِwَٰjgَtُّm", "root": "جور"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَجَنَّٰتٌ", "translit": "ٌtَّٰnَjgَw", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَعْنَٰبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَٰnْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عنب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَزَرْعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعْrَzَw", "root": "زرع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَنَخِيلٌ", "translit": "ٌlyِhkَnَw", "root": "نخل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "صِنْوَانٌ", "translit": "ٌnāَwْnِṣ", "root": "صنو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَغَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَغَw", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "صِنْوَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَwْnِṣ", "root": "صنو"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يُسْقَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَqْsُy", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِمَآءٍ", "translit": "ٍءٓāَmِb", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَٰحِدٍ", "translit": "ٍdِḥَٰw", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَنُفَضِّلُ", "translit": "ُlِّḍَfُnَw", "root": "فضل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بَعْضَهَا", "translit": "āَhَḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "بَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلْأُكُلِ", "translit": "ِlُkُaʾْlٱ", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "لَءَايَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "لِّقَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَqِّl", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "يَعْقِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِqْʿعَy", "root": "عقل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَإِن تَعْجَبْ فَعَجَبٌ قَوْلُهُمْ أَءِذَا كُنَّا تُرَٰبًا أَءِنَّا لَفِى خَلْقٍ جَدِيدٍۗ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ بِرَبِّهِمْۖ وَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلْأَغْلَٰلُ فِىٓ أَعْنَاقِهِمْۖ وَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلنَّارِۖ هُمْ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ", "translation": "And if you are astonished,[1] [O Muḥammad] - then astonishing is their saying, \"When we are dust, will we indeed be [brought] into a new creation?\" Those are the ones who have disbelieved in their Lord, and those will have shackles[2] upon their necks, and those are the companions of the Fire; they will abide therein eternally.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَعْجَبْ", "translit": "ْbَjgْʿعَt", "root": "عجب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَعَجَبٌ", "translit": "ٌbَjgَʿعَf", "root": "عجب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَوْلُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُlْwَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَءِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تُرَٰبًا", "translit": "āًbَٰrُt", "root": "ترب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَءِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "خَلْقٍ", "translit": "ٍqْlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "جَدِيدٍ", "translit": "ٍdyِdَjg", "root": "جدد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِرَبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْأَغْلَٰلُ", "translit": "ُlَٰlْغَaʾْlٱ", "root": "غلل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَعْنَاقِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِqāَnْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عنق"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "خَٰلِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِlَٰhk", "root": "خلد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَيَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ بِٱلسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ ٱلْحَسَنَةِ وَقَدْ خَلَتْ مِن قَبْلِهِمُ ٱلْمَثُلَٰتُۗ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو مَغْفِرَةٍ لِّلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ ظُلْمِهِمْۖ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَشَدِيدُ ٱلْعِقَابِ ", "translation": "They impatiently urge you to bring about evil before good,[1] while there has already occurred before them similar punishments [to what they demand]. And indeed, your Lord is the possessor of forgiveness for the people despite their wrongdoing, and indeed, your Lord is severe in penalty.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ", "translit": "َkَnwُlِjgْʿعَtْsَyَw", "root": "عجل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِٱلسَّيِّئَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَyʾِّyَّslٱِb", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَبْلَ", "translit": "َlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْحَسَنَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَnَsَḥْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خَلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَhk", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْمَثُلَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰlُhtَmْlٱ", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَذُو", "translit": "wُhdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مَغْفِرَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَrِfْغَm", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لِّلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlِّl", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ظُلْمِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِmْlُẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَشَدِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِdَhsَl", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْعِقَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَqِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عقب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَيَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَوْلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيْهِ ءَايَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦٓۗ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مُنذِرٌۖ وَلِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ هَادٍ ", "translation": "And those who disbelieved say, \"Why has a sign not been sent down to him from his Lord?\" You are only a warner, and for every people is a guide.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ءَايَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُنذِرٌ", "translit": "ٌrِhdnُm", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَلِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِlَw", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "قَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "هَادٍ", "translit": "ٍdāَh", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "ٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ أُنثَىٰ وَمَا تَغِيضُ ٱلْأَرْحَامُ وَمَا تَزْدَادُۖ وَكُلُّ شَىْءٍ عِندَهُۥ بِمِقْدَارٍ ", "translation": "Allāh knows what every female carries[1] and what the wombs lose [prematurely] or exceed.[2] And everything with Him is by due measure.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَحْمِلُ", "translit": "ُlِmْḥَt", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُلُّ", "translit": "ُّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُنثَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَhtnُaʾ", "root": "انث"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَغِيضُ", "translit": "ُḍyِغَt", "root": "غيض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْحَامُ", "translit": "ُmāَḥْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَزْدَادُ", "translit": "ُdāَdْzَt", "root": "زيد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَكُلُّ", "translit": "ُّlُkَw", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عِندَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِمِقْدَارٍ", "translit": "ٍrāَdْqِmِb", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "عَٰلِمُ ٱلْغَيْبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ ٱلْكَبِيرُ ٱلْمُتَعَالِ ", "translation": "[He is] Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, the Grand, the Exalted.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَٰلِمُ", "translit": "ُmِlَٰʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَdَٰhَّhslٱَw", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْكَبِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِbَkْlٱ", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُتَعَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَʿعَtُmْlٱ", "root": "علو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "سَوَآءٌ مِّنكُم مَّنْ أَسَرَّ ٱلْقَوْلَ وَمَن جَهَرَ بِهِۦ وَمَنْ هُوَ مُسْتَخْفٍۭ بِٱلَّيْلِ وَسَارِبٌۢ بِٱلنَّهَارِ ", "translation": "It is the same [to Him] concerning you whether one conceals [his] speech or publicizes it and whether one is hidden by night or conspicuous [among others] by day.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَوَآءٌ", "translit": "ٌءٓāَwَs", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّنكُم", "translit": "mُknِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّنْ", "translit": "ْnَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَسَرَّ", "translit": "َّrَsَaʾ", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْلَ", "translit": "َlْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "جَهَرَ", "translit": "َrَhَjg", "root": "جهر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُسْتَخْفٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭfْhkَtْsُm", "root": "خفي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱِb", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَسَارِبٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢbِrāَsَw", "root": "سرب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِٱلنَّهَارِ", "translit": "ِrāَhَّnlٱِb", "root": "نهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "لَهُۥ مُعَقِّبَٰتٌ مِّنۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِۦ يَحْفَظُونَهُۥ مِنْ أَمْرِ ٱللَّهِۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُغَيِّرُ مَا بِقَوْمٍ حَتَّىٰ يُغَيِّرُوا۟ مَا بِأَنفُسِهِمْۗ وَإِذَآ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ بِقَوْمٍ سُوٓءًا فَلَا مَرَدَّ لَهُۥۚ وَمَا لَهُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَالٍ ", "translation": "For him [i.e., each one] are successive [angels][1] before and behind him who protect him by the decree of Allāh.[2] Indeed, Allāh will not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves. And when Allāh intends for a people ill,[3] there is no repelling it. And there is not for them besides Him any patron.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُعَقِّبَٰتٌ", "translit": "ٌtَٰbِّqَʿعُm", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمِنْ", "translit": "ْnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خَلْفِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِfْlَhk", "root": "خلف"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَحْفَظُونَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnwُẓَfْḥَy", "root": "حفظ"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَمْرِ", "translit": "ِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُغَيِّرُ", "translit": "ُrِّyَغُy", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِقَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَqِb", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يُغَيِّرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrِّyَغُy", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِأَنفُسِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِsُfnَaʾِb", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَإِذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَرَادَ", "translit": "َdāَrَaʾ", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "بِقَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَqِb", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "سُوٓءًا", "translit": "āًءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "مَرَدَّ", "translit": "َّdَrَm", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "وَالٍ", "translit": "ٍlāَw", "root": "ولي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "هُوَ ٱلَّذِى يُرِيكُمُ ٱلْبَرْقَ خَوْفًا وَطَمَعًا وَيُنشِئُ ٱلسَّحَابَ ٱلثِّقَالَ ", "translation": "It is He who shows you lightning, [causing] fear and aspiration, and generates the heavy clouds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُرِيكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkyِrُy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَرْقَ", "translit": "َqْrَbْlٱ", "root": "برق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "خَوْفًا", "translit": "āًfْwَhk", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَطَمَعًا", "translit": "āًʿعَmَṭَw", "root": "طمع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَيُنشِئُ", "translit": "ُyʾِhsnُyَw", "root": "نشا"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلسَّحَابَ", "translit": "َbāَḥَّslٱ", "root": "سحب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلثِّقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqِّhtlٱ", "root": "ثقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "وَيُسَبِّحُ ٱلرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهِۦ وَٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ مِنْ خِيفَتِهِۦ وَيُرْسِلُ ٱلصَّوَٰعِقَ فَيُصِيبُ بِهَا مَن يَشَآءُ وَهُمْ يُجَٰدِلُونَ فِى ٱللَّهِ وَهُوَ شَدِيدُ ٱلْمِحَالِ ", "translation": "And the thunder exalts [Allāh] with praise of Him - and the angels [as well] from fear of Him - and He sends thunderbolts and strikes therewith whom He wills while they dispute about Allāh; and He is severe in assault.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيُسَبِّحُ", "translit": "ُḥِّbَsُyَw", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلرَّعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْʿعَّrlٱ", "root": "رعد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِحَمْدِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِdْmَḥِb", "root": "حمد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱَw", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خِيفَتِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِtَfyِhk", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَيُرْسِلُ", "translit": "ُlِsْrُyَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلصَّوَٰعِقَ", "translit": "َqِʿعَٰwَّṣlٱ", "root": "صعق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَيُصِيبُ", "translit": "ُbyِṣُyَf", "root": "صوب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِهَا", "translit": "āَhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يُجَٰدِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِdَٰjgُy", "root": "جدل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "شَدِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِdَhs", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْمِحَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَḥِmْlٱ", "root": "محل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "لَهُۥ دَعْوَةُ ٱلْحَقِّۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِهِۦ لَا يَسْتَجِيبُونَ لَهُم بِشَىْءٍ إِلَّا كَبَٰسِطِ كَفَّيْهِ إِلَى ٱلْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُغَ فَاهُ وَمَا هُوَ بِبَٰلِغِهِۦۚ وَمَا دُعَآءُ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِى ضَلَٰلٍ ", "translation": "To Him [alone] is the supplication of truth. And those they call upon besides Him do not respond to them with a thing, except as one who stretches his hands toward water [from afar, calling it] to reach his mouth, but it will not reach it [thus].[1] And the supplication of the disbelievers is not but in error [i.e., futility].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَعْوَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَwْʿعَd", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَدْعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعْdَy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَسْتَجِيبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbyِjgَtْsَy", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِشَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhsِb", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "كَبَٰسِطِ", "translit": "ِṭِsَٰbَk", "root": "بسط"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَفَّيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَّfَk", "root": "كفف"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmْlٱ", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لِيَبْلُغَ", "translit": "َغُlْbَyِl", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَf", "root": "فوه"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِبَٰلِغِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِغِlَٰbِb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "دُعَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَʿعُd", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "وَلِلَّهِ يَسْجُدُ مَن فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ طَوْعًا وَكَرْهًا وَظِلَٰلُهُم بِٱلْغُدُوِّ وَٱلْءَاصَالِ۩ ", "translation": "And to Allāh prostrates whoever is within the heavens and the earth, willingly or by compulsion, and their shadows [as well] in the mornings and the afternoons.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِlَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْجُدُ", "translit": "ُdُjgْsَy", "root": "سجد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "طَوْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْwَṭ", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَكَرْهًا", "translit": "āًhْrَkَw", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَظِلَٰلُهُم", "translit": "mُhُlَٰlِẓَw", "root": "ظلل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِٱلْغُدُوِّ", "translit": "ِّwُdُغْlٱِb", "root": "غدو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱلْءَاصَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَṣāَءْlٱَw", "root": "اصل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "قُلْ مَن رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ قُلِ ٱللَّهُۚ قُلْ أَفَٱتَّخَذْتُم مِّن دُونِهِۦٓ أَوْلِيَآءَ لَا يَمْلِكُونَ لِأَنفُسِهِمْ نَفْعًا وَلَا ضَرًّاۚ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى ٱلْأَعْمَىٰ وَٱلْبَصِيرُ أَمْ هَلْ تَسْتَوِى ٱلظُّلُمَٰتُ وَٱلنُّورُۗ أَمْ جَعَلُوا۟ لِلَّهِ شُرَكَآءَ خَلَقُوا۟ كَخَلْقِهِۦ فَتَشَٰبَهَ ٱلْخَلْقُ عَلَيْهِمْۚ قُلِ ٱللَّهُ خَٰلِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَهُوَ ٱلْوَٰحِدُ ٱلْقَهَّٰرُ ", "translation": "Say, \"Who is Lord of the heavens and earth?\" Say, \"Allāh.\" Say, \"Have you then taken besides Him allies not possessing [even] for themselves any benefit or any harm?\" Say, \"Is the blind equivalent to the seeing? Or is darkness equivalent to light? Or have they attributed to Allāh partners who created like His creation so that the creation [of each] seemed similar to them?\"[1] Say, \"Allāh is the Creator of all things, and He is the One, the Prevailing.\"[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَّبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قُلِ", "translit": "ِlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَفَٱتَّخَذْتُم", "translit": "mُtْhdَhkَّtٱَfَaʾ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَوْلِيَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَyِlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَمْلِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِlْmَy", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لِأَنفُسِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِsُfnَaʾِl", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "نَفْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْfَn", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ضَرًّا", "translit": "āًّrَḍ", "root": "ضرر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يَسْتَوِى", "translit": "àِwَtْsَy", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْأَعْمَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَmْʿعَaʾْlٱ", "root": "عمي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَٱلْبَصِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِṣَbْlٱَw", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "تَسْتَوِى", "translit": "àِwَtْsَt", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلظُّلُمَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰmُlُّẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "وَٱلنُّورُ", "translit": "ُrwُّnlٱَw", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "جَعَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "شُرَكَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَkَrُhs", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "خَلَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "كَخَلْقِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِqْlَhkَk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "فَتَشَٰبَهَ", "translit": "َhَbَٰhsَtَf", "root": "شبه"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "ٱلْخَلْقُ", "translit": "ُqْlَhkْlٱ", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "قُلِ", "translit": "ِlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "خَٰلِقُ", "translit": "ُqِlَٰhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "ٱلْوَٰحِدُ", "translit": "ُdِḥَٰwْlٱ", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "ٱلْقَهَّٰرُ", "translit": "ُrَّٰhَqْlٱ", "root": "قهر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "أَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَسَالَتْ أَوْدِيَةٌۢ بِقَدَرِهَا فَٱحْتَمَلَ ٱلسَّيْلُ زَبَدًا رَّابِيًاۚ وَمِمَّا يُوقِدُونَ عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلنَّارِ ٱبْتِغَآءَ حِلْيَةٍ أَوْ مَتَٰعٍ زَبَدٌ مِّثْلُهُۥۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْحَقَّ وَٱلْبَٰطِلَۚ فَأَمَّا ٱلزَّبَدُ فَيَذْهَبُ جُفَآءًۖ وَأَمَّا مَا يَنفَعُ ٱلنَّاسَ فَيَمْكُثُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَضْرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْأَمْثَالَ ", "translation": "He sends down from the sky, rain, and valleys flow according to their capacity, and the torrent carries a rising foam. And from that [ore] which they heat in the fire, desiring adornments and utensils, is a foam like it. Thus Allāh presents [the example of] truth and falsehood. As for the foam, it vanishes, [being] cast off; but as for that which benefits the people, it remains on the earth. Thus does Allāh present examples.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَنزَلَ", "translit": "َlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَm", "root": "موه"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَسَالَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlāَsَf", "root": "سيل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَوْدِيَةٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢẗَyِdْwَaʾ", "root": "ودي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِقَدَرِهَا", "translit": "āَhِrَdَqِb", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَٱحْتَمَلَ", "translit": "َlَmَtْḥٱَf", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلسَّيْلُ", "translit": "ُlْyَّslٱ", "root": "سيل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "زَبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbَz", "root": "زبد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَّابِيًا", "translit": "āًyِbāَّr", "root": "ربو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يُوقِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِqwُy", "root": "وقد"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱبْتِغَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَغِtْbٱ", "root": "بغي"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "حِلْيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyْlِḥ", "root": "حلي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مَتَٰعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعَٰtَm", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "زَبَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَbَz", "root": "زبد"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "مِّثْلُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُlْhtِّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَضْرِبُ", "translit": "ُbِrْḍَy", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَٱلْبَٰطِلَ", "translit": "َlِṭَٰbْlٱَw", "root": "بطل"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "فَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "ٱلزَّبَدُ", "translit": "ُdَbَّzlٱ", "root": "زبد"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "فَيَذْهَبُ", "translit": "ُbَhْhdَyَf", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "جُفَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَfُjg", "root": "جفا"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "يَنفَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَfnَy", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسَ", "translit": "َsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "فَيَمْكُثُ", "translit": "ُhtُkْmَyَf", "root": "مكث"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "يَضْرِبُ", "translit": "ُbِrْḍَy", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْثَالَ", "translit": "َlāَhtْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "مثل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "لِلَّذِينَ ٱسْتَجَابُوا۟ لِرَبِّهِمُ ٱلْحُسْنَىٰۚ وَٱلَّذِينَ لَمْ يَسْتَجِيبُوا۟ لَهُۥ لَوْ أَنَّ لَهُم مَّا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا وَمِثْلَهُۥ مَعَهُۥ لَٱفْتَدَوْا۟ بِهِۦٓۚ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ سُوٓءُ ٱلْحِسَابِ وَمَأْوَىٰهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۖ وَبِئْسَ ٱلْمِهَادُ ", "translation": "For those who have responded to their Lord is the best [reward], but those who did not respond to Him - if they had all that is in the earth entirely and the like of it with it, they would [attempt to] ransom themselves thereby. Those will have the worst account, and their refuge is Hell, and wretched is the resting place.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱسْتَجَابُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbāَjgَtْsٱ", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِرَبِّهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhِّbَrِl", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْsُḥْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَسْتَجِيبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbyِjgَtْsَy", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًʿعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَمِثْلَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَlْhtِmَw", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مَعَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "لَٱفْتَدَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَdَtْfٱَl", "root": "فدي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "سُوٓءُ", "translit": "ُءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلْحِسَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَsِḥْlٱ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَمَأْوَىٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhٰàَwْaʾَmَw", "root": "اوي"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "جَهَنَّمُ", "translit": "ُmَّnَhَjg", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "وَبِئْسَ", "translit": "َsْyʾِbَw", "root": "باس"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْمِهَادُ", "translit": "ُdāَhِmْlٱ", "root": "مهد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "أَفَمَن يَعْلَمُ أَنَّمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ ٱلْحَقُّ كَمَنْ هُوَ أَعْمَىٰٓۚ إِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ أُو۟لُوا۟ ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ ", "translation": "Then is he who knows that what has been revealed to you from your Lord is the truth like one who is blind? They will only be reminded who are people of understanding -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَمَن", "translit": "nَmَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَّبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَعْمَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَتَذَكَّرُ", "translit": "ُrَّkَhdَtَy", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أُو۟لُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰbْlَaʾْlٱ", "root": "لبب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ يُوفُونَ بِعَهْدِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا يَنقُضُونَ ٱلْمِيثَٰقَ ", "translation": "Those who fulfill the covenant of Allāh and do not break the contract,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُوفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfwُy", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِعَهْدِ", "translit": "ِdْhَʿعِb", "root": "عهد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَنقُضُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḍُqnَy", "root": "نقض"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْمِيثَٰقَ", "translit": "َqَٰhtyِmْlٱ", "root": "وثق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ يَصِلُونَ مَآ أَمَرَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِۦٓ أَن يُوصَلَ وَيَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ وَيَخَافُونَ سُوٓءَ ٱلْحِسَابِ ", "translation": "And those who join that which Allāh has ordered to be joined[1] and fear their Lord and are afraid of the evil of [their] account,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَصِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِṣَy", "root": "وصل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمَرَ", "translit": "َrَmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُوصَلَ", "translit": "َlَṣwُy", "root": "وصل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَيَخْشَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَhsْhkَyَw", "root": "خشي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَيَخَافُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfāَhkَyَw", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "سُوٓءَ", "translit": "َءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْحِسَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَsِḥْlٱ", "root": "حسب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُوا۟ ٱبْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ رَبِّهِمْ وَأَقَامُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنفَقُوا۟ مِمَّا رَزَقْنَٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَعَلَانِيَةً وَيَدْرَءُونَ بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عُقْبَى ٱلدَّارِ ", "translation": "And those who are patient, seeking the face [i.e., acceptance] of their Lord, and establish prayer and spend from what We have provided for them secretly and publicly and prevent evil with good - those will have the good consequence of [this] home[1] -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَبَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَbَṣ", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱبْتِغَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَغِtْbٱ", "root": "بغي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَجْهِ", "translit": "ِhْjgَw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَقَامُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmāَqَaʾَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ", "translit": "َẗٰwَlَّṣlٱ", "root": "صلو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَنفَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَfnَaʾَw", "root": "نفق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَزَقْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْqَzَr", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "سِرًّا", "translit": "āًّrِs", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَعَلَانِيَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyِnāَlَʿعَw", "root": "علن"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَيَدْرَءُونَ", "translit": "َnwُءَrْdَyَw", "root": "درا"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَnَsَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلسَّيِّئَةَ", "translit": "َẗَyʾِّyَّslٱ", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "عُقْبَى", "translit": "àَbْqُʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلدَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّdlٱ", "root": "دور"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "جَنَّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَدْخُلُونَهَا وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنْ ءَابَآئِهِمْ وَأَزْوَٰجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمْۖ وَٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يَدْخُلُونَ عَلَيْهِم مِّن كُلِّ بَابٍ ", "translation": "Gardens of perpetual residence; they will enter them with whoever were righteous among their forefathers, their spouses and their descendants. And the angels will enter upon them from every gate, [saying],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَدْنٍ", "translit": "ٍnْdَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَدْخُلُونَهَا", "translit": "āَhَnwُlُhkْdَy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "صَلَحَ", "translit": "َḥَlَṣ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ءَابَآئِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِyʾٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَزْوَٰجِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِjgَٰwْzَaʾَw", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَّٰyِّrُhdَw", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱَw", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَدْخُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُhkْdَy", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَb", "root": "بوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيْكُم بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْۚ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى ٱلدَّارِ ", "translation": "\"Peace [i.e., security] be upon you for what you patiently endured.\" And excellent is the final home.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُم", "translit": "mُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "صَبَرْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْrَbَṣ", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَنِعْمَ", "translit": "َmْʿعِnَf", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عُقْبَى", "translit": "àَbْqُʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلدَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّdlٱ", "root": "دور"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ يَنقُضُونَ عَهْدَ ٱللَّهِ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مِيثَٰقِهِۦ وَيَقْطَعُونَ مَآ أَمَرَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِۦٓ أَن يُوصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِۙ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمُ ٱللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوٓءُ ٱلدَّارِ ", "translation": "But those who break the covenant of Allāh after contracting it and sever that which Allāh has ordered to be joined and spread corruption on earth - for them is the curse, and they will have the worst home.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنقُضُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḍُqnَy", "root": "نقض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَهْدَ", "translit": "َdْhَʿع", "root": "عهد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِيثَٰقِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِqَٰhtyِm", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَيَقْطَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَṭْqَyَw", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَمَرَ", "translit": "َrَmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يُوصَلَ", "translit": "َlَṣwُy", "root": "وصل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَيُفْسِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِsْfُyَw", "root": "فسد"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّعْنَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَnْʿعَّllٱ", "root": "لعن"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "سُوٓءُ", "translit": "ُءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلدَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّdlٱ", "root": "دور"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "ٱللَّهُ يَبْسُطُ ٱلرِّزْقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُۚ وَفَرِحُوا۟ بِٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا وَمَا ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَا فِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ إِلَّا مَتَٰعٌ ", "translation": "Allāh extends provision for whom He wills and restricts [it]. And they rejoice in the worldly life, while the worldly life is not, compared to the Hereafter, except [brief] enjoyment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَبْسُطُ", "translit": "ُṭُsْbَy", "root": "بسط"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلرِّزْقَ", "translit": "َqْzِّrlٱ", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِمَن", "translit": "nَmِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَيَقْدِرُ", "translit": "ُrِdْqَyَw", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَفَرِحُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḥِrَfَw", "root": "فرح"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَيَوٰةِ", "translit": "ِẗٰwَyَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ", "translit": "ُẗٰwَyَḥْlٱ", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مَتَٰعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعَٰtَm", "root": "متع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "وَيَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَوْلَآ أُنزِلَ عَلَيْهِ ءَايَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦۗ قُلْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُضِلُّ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىٓ إِلَيْهِ مَنْ أَنَابَ ", "translation": "And those who disbelieved say, \"Why has a sign not been sent down to him from his Lord?\" Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Indeed, Allāh leaves astray whom He wills and guides to Himself whoever turns back [to Him] -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ءَايَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَّبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يُضِلُّ", "translit": "ُّlِḍُy", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَيَهْدِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِdْhَyَw", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَنَابَ", "translit": "َbāَnَaʾ", "root": "نوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَتَطْمَئِنُّ قُلُوبُهُم بِذِكْرِ ٱللَّهِۗ أَلَا بِذِكْرِ ٱللَّهِ تَطْمَئِنُّ ٱلْقُلُوبُ ", "translation": "Those who have believed and whose hearts are assured by the remembrance of Allāh. Unquestionably, by the remembrance of Allāh hearts are assured.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَتَطْمَئِنُّ", "translit": "ُّnِyʾَmْṭَtَw", "root": "طمان"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قُلُوبُهُم", "translit": "mُhُbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِذِكْرِ", "translit": "ِrْkِhdِb", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِذِكْرِ", "translit": "ِrْkِhdِb", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "تَطْمَئِنُّ", "translit": "ُّnِyʾَmْṭَt", "root": "طمان"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْقُلُوبُ", "translit": "ُbwُlُqْlٱ", "root": "قلب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ طُوبَىٰ لَهُمْ وَحُسْنُ مَـَٔابٍ ", "translation": "Those who have believed and done righteous deeds - a good state is theirs and a good return.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "طُوبَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَbwُṭ", "root": "طيب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَحُسْنُ", "translit": "ُnْsُḥَw", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَـَٔابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَٔـَm", "root": "اوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "كَذَٰلِكَ أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ فِىٓ أُمَّةٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِن قَبْلِهَآ أُمَمٌ لِّتَتْلُوَا۟ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَيْكَ وَهُمْ يَكْفُرُونَ بِٱلرَّحْمَٰنِۚ قُلْ هُوَ رَبِّى لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَإِلَيْهِ مَتَابِ ", "translation": "Thus have We sent you to a community before which [other] communities have passed on so you might recite to them that which We revealed to you, while they disbelieve in the Most Merciful. Say, \"He is my Lord; there is no deity except Him. Upon Him I rely, and to Him is my return.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ", "translit": "َkَٰnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أُمَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خَلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَhk", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَبْلِهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أُمَمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِّتَتْلُوَا۟", "translit": "۟āَwُlْtَtِّl", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَوْحَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَḥْwَaʾ", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَكْفُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُfْkَy", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ", "translit": "ِnَٰmْḥَّrlٱِb", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِلَٰهَ", "translit": "َhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "تَوَكَّلْتُ", "translit": "ُtْlَّkَwَt", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَإِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "مَتَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَtَm", "root": "توب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "وَلَوْ أَنَّ قُرْءَانًا سُيِّرَتْ بِهِ ٱلْجِبَالُ أَوْ قُطِّعَتْ بِهِ ٱلْأَرْضُ أَوْ كُلِّمَ بِهِ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰۗ بَل لِّلَّهِ ٱلْأَمْرُ جَمِيعًاۗ أَفَلَمْ يَا۟يْـَٔسِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ أَن لَّوْ يَشَآءُ ٱللَّهُ لَهَدَى ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعًاۗ وَلَا يَزَالُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ تُصِيبُهُم بِمَا صَنَعُوا۟ قَارِعَةٌ أَوْ تَحُلُّ قَرِيبًا مِّن دَارِهِمْ حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِىَ وَعْدُ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُخْلِفُ ٱلْمِيعَادَ ", "translation": "And if there was any Qur’ān [i.e., recitation] by which the mountains would be removed or the earth would be broken apart or the dead would be made to speak,[1] [it would be this Qur’ān], but to Allāh belongs the affair entirely. Then have those who believed not accepted that had Allāh willed, He would have guided the people, all of them? And those who disbelieve do not cease to be struck, for what they have done, by calamity - or it will descend near their home - until there comes the promise of Allāh. Indeed, Allāh does not fail in [His] promise.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قُرْءَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَءْrُq", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سُيِّرَتْ", "translit": "ْtَrِّyُs", "root": "سير"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهِ", "translit": "ِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْجِبَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَbِjgْlٱ", "root": "جبل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قُطِّعَتْ", "translit": "ْtَʿعِّṭُq", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِهِ", "translit": "ِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كُلِّمَ", "translit": "َmِّlُk", "root": "كلم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِهِ", "translit": "ِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَtْwَmْlٱ", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بَل", "translit": "lَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لِّلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِّl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًʿعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَفَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يَا۟يْـَٔسِ", "translit": "ِsَٔـْy۟āَy", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "لَّوْ", "translit": "ْwَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لَهَدَى", "translit": "àَdَhَl", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسَ", "translit": "َsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًʿعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "يَزَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَzَy", "root": "زيل"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "تُصِيبُهُم", "translit": "mُhُbyِṣُt", "root": "صوب"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "صَنَعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعَnَṣ", "root": "صنع"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "قَارِعَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَʿعِrāَq", "root": "قرع"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "تَحُلُّ", "translit": "ُّlُḥَt", "root": "حلل"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "قَرِيبًا", "translit": "āًbyِrَq", "root": "قرب"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "دَارِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِrāَd", "root": "دور"}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "يَأْتِىَ", "translit": "َàِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "وَعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْʿعَw", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 46, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 47, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 48, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 49, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 50, "arabic": "يُخْلِفُ", "translit": "ُfِlْhkُy", "root": "خلف"}, {"id": 51, "arabic": "ٱلْمِيعَادَ", "translit": "َdāَʿعyِmْlٱ", "root": "وعد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "وَلَقَدِ ٱسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّن قَبْلِكَ فَأَمْلَيْتُ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ ثُمَّ أَخَذْتُهُمْۖ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ ", "translation": "And already were [other] messengers ridiculed before you, and I extended the time of those who disbelieved; then I seized them, and how [terrible] was My penalty.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدِ", "translit": "ِdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱسْتُهْزِئَ", "translit": "َyʾِzْhُtْsٱ", "root": "هزا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِرُسُلٍ", "translit": "ٍlُsُrِb", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَبْلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَأَمْلَيْتُ", "translit": "ُtْyَlْmَaʾَf", "root": "ملو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَخَذْتُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُtْhdَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَكَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَkَf", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عِقَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَqِʿع", "root": "عقب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "أَفَمَنْ هُوَ قَآئِمٌ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ نَفْسٍۭ بِمَا كَسَبَتْۗ وَجَعَلُوا۟ لِلَّهِ شُرَكَآءَ قُلْ سَمُّوهُمْۚ أَمْ تُنَبِّـُٔونَهُۥ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ أَم بِظَٰهِرٍ مِّنَ ٱلْقَوْلِۗ بَلْ زُيِّنَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مَكْرُهُمْ وَصُدُّوا۟ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِۗ وَمَن يُضْلِلِ ٱللَّهُ فَمَا لَهُۥ مِنْ هَادٍ ", "translation": "Then is He who is a maintainer of every soul, [knowing] what it has earned, [like any other]? But to Allāh they have attributed partners. Say, \"Name them. Or do you inform Him of that[1] which He knows not upon the earth or of what is apparent [i.e., alleged] of speech?\"[2] Rather, their [own] plan has been made attractive to those who disbelieve, and they have been averted from the way. And whomever Allāh sends astray - there will be for him no guide.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَآئِمٌ", "translit": "ٌmِyʾٓāَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَفْسٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَسَبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَsَk", "root": "كسب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَجَعَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "شُرَكَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَkَrُhs", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سَمُّوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُّmَs", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "تُنَبِّـُٔونَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnwُٔـِّbَnُt", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَم", "translit": "mَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِظَٰهِرٍ", "translit": "ٍrِhَٰẓِb", "root": "ظهر"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْلِ", "translit": "ِlْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "زُيِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّyُz", "root": "زين"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "مَكْرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُrْkَm", "root": "مكر"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "وَصُدُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّdُṣَw", "root": "صدد"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "ٱلسَّبِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِbَّslٱ", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "يُضْلِلِ", "translit": "ِlِlْḍُy", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "هَادٍ", "translit": "ٍdāَh", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "لَّهُمْ عَذَابٌ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَاۖ وَلَعَذَابُ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ أَشَقُّۖ وَمَا لَهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن وَاقٍ ", "translation": "For them will be punishment in the life of [this] world, and the punishment of the Hereafter is more severe. And they will not have from Allāh any protector.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَذَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ", "translit": "ِẗٰwَyَḥْlٱ", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَعَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿعَlَw", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَشَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَhsَaʾ", "root": "شقق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَاقٍ", "translit": "ٍqāَw", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "مَّثَلُ ٱلْجَنَّةِ ٱلَّتِى وُعِدَ ٱلْمُتَّقُونَۖ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُۖ أُكُلُهَا دَآئِمٌ وَظِلُّهَاۚ تِلْكَ عُقْبَى ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوا۟ۖ وَّعُقْبَى ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ ٱلنَّارُ ", "translation": "The example [i.e., description] of Paradise, which the righteous have been promised, is [that] beneath it rivers flow. Its fruit is lasting, and its shade. That is the consequence for the righteous, and the consequence for the disbelievers is the Fire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَّثَلُ", "translit": "ُlَhtَّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وُعِدَ", "translit": "َdِʿعُw", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtُmْlٱ", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَجْرِى", "translit": "àِrْjgَt", "root": "جري"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَحْتِهَا", "translit": "āَhِtْḥَt", "root": "تحت"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ", "translit": "ُrَٰhْnَaʾْlٱ", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أُكُلُهَا", "translit": "āَhُlُkُaʾ", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "دَآئِمٌ", "translit": "ٌmِyʾٓāَd", "root": "دوم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَظِلُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّlِẓَw", "root": "ظلل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِt", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عُقْبَى", "translit": "àَbْqُʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱتَّقَوا۟", "translit": "۟āwَqَّtٱ", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَّعُقْبَى", "translit": "àَbْqُʿعَّw", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارُ", "translit": "ُrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَاتَيْنَٰهُمُ ٱلْكِتَٰبَ يَفْرَحُونَ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَۖ وَمِنَ ٱلْأَحْزَابِ مَن يُنكِرُ بَعْضَهُۥۚ قُلْ إِنَّمَآ أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أَعْبُدَ ٱللَّهَ وَلَآ أُشْرِكَ بِهِۦٓۚ إِلَيْهِ أَدْعُوا۟ وَإِلَيْهِ مَـَٔابِ ", "translation": "And [the believers among] those to whom We have given the [previous] Scripture rejoice at what has been revealed to you, [O Muḥammad], but among the [opposing] factions are those who deny part of it [i.e., the Qur’ān]. Say, \"I have only been commanded to worship Allāh and not associate [anything] with Him. To Him I invite, and to Him is my return.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْنَٰهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَٰnْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبَ", "translit": "َbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَفْرَحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥَrْfَy", "root": "فرح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحْزَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَzْḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حزب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُنكِرُ", "translit": "ُrِknُy", "root": "نكر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَعْضَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أُمِرْتُ", "translit": "ُtْrِmُaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَعْبُدَ", "translit": "َdُbْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أُشْرِكَ", "translit": "َkِrْhsُaʾ", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعْdَaʾ", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَإِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مَـَٔابِ", "translit": "ِbāَٔـَm", "root": "اوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ أَنزَلْنَٰهُ حُكْمًا عَرَبِيًّاۚ وَلَئِنِ ٱتَّبَعْتَ أَهْوَآءَهُم بَعْدَمَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ ٱلْعِلْمِ مَا لَكَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن وَلِىٍّ وَلَا وَاقٍ ", "translation": "And thus We have revealed it as an Arabic legislation.[1] And if you should follow their inclinations after what has come to you of knowledge, you would not have against Allāh any ally or any protector.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنزَلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حُكْمًا", "translit": "āًmْkُḥ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَرَبِيًّا", "translit": "āًّyِbَrَʿع", "root": "عرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَئِنِ", "translit": "ِnِyʾَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعْتَ", "translit": "َtْʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَهْوَآءَهُم", "translit": "mُhَءٓāَwْhَaʾ", "root": "هوي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَعْدَمَا", "translit": "āَmَdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "جَآءَكَ", "translit": "َkَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعِلْمِ", "translit": "ِmْlِʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلِىٍّ", "translit": "ٍّàِlَw", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَاقٍ", "translit": "ٍqāَw", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّن قَبْلِكَ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ أَزْوَٰجًا وَذُرِّيَّةًۚ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُولٍ أَن يَأْتِىَ بِـَٔايَةٍ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِ ٱللَّهِۗ لِكُلِّ أَجَلٍ كِتَابٌ ", "translation": "And We have already sent messengers before you and assigned to them wives and descendants. And it was not for a messenger to come with a sign except by permission of Allāh. For every term is a decree.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رُسُلًا", "translit": "āًlُsُr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَبْلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَجَعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَزْوَٰجًا", "translit": "āًjgَٰwْzَaʾ", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَذُرِّيَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّyِّrُhdَw", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لِرَسُولٍ", "translit": "ٍlwُsَrِl", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَأْتِىَ", "translit": "َàِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِـَٔايَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyāَٔـِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِإِذْنِ", "translit": "ِnْhdِiʾِb", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِl", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أَجَلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَjgَaʾ", "root": "اجل"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "كِتَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَtِk", "root": "كتب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "يَمْحُوا۟ ٱللَّهُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيُثْبِتُۖ وَعِندَهُۥٓ أُمُّ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ", "translation": "Allāh eliminates what He wills or confirms, and with Him is the Mother of the Book.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَمْحُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḥْmَy", "root": "محو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَيُثْبِتُ", "translit": "ُtِbْhtُyَw", "root": "ثبت"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَعِندَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَdnِʿعَw", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أُمُّ", "translit": "ُّmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "وَإِن مَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ ٱلَّذِى نَعِدُهُمْ أَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ ٱلْبَلَٰغُ وَعَلَيْنَا ٱلْحِسَابُ ", "translation": "And whether We show you part of what We promise them or take you in death, upon you is only the [duty of] notification, and upon Us is the account.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُرِيَنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnَyِrُn", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضَ", "translit": "َḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَعِدُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُdِʿعَn", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnَyَّfَwَtَn", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَإِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْبَلَٰغُ", "translit": "ُغَٰlَbْlٱ", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَعَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْحِسَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَsِḥْlٱ", "root": "حسب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّا نَأْتِى ٱلْأَرْضَ نَنقُصُهَا مِنْ أَطْرَافِهَاۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَحْكُمُ لَا مُعَقِّبَ لِحُكْمِهِۦۚ وَهُوَ سَرِيعُ ٱلْحِسَابِ ", "translation": "Have they not seen that We set upon the land, reducing it from its borders?[1] And Allāh decides; there is no adjuster of His decision. And He is swift in account.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَرَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَأْتِى", "translit": "àِtْaʾَn", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَنقُصُهَا", "translit": "āَhُṣُqnَn", "root": "نقص"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَطْرَافِهَا", "translit": "āَhِfāَrْṭَaʾ", "root": "طرف"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَحْكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkْḥَy", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُعَقِّبَ", "translit": "َbِّqَʿعُm", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لِحُكْمِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِmْkُḥِl", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سَرِيعُ", "translit": "ُʿعyِrَs", "root": "سرع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْحِسَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَsِḥْlٱ", "root": "حسب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "وَقَدْ مَكَرَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ فَلِلَّهِ ٱلْمَكْرُ جَمِيعًاۖ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْسِبُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍۗ وَسَيَعْلَمُ ٱلْكُفَّٰرُ لِمَنْ عُقْبَى ٱلدَّارِ ", "translation": "And those before them had plotted, but to Allāh belongs the plan entirely. He knows what every soul earns, and the disbelievers will know for whom is the final home.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَكَرَ", "translit": "َrَkَm", "root": "مكر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَلِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِlَf", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْمَكْرُ", "translit": "ُrْkَmْlٱ", "root": "مكر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًʿعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَكْسِبُ", "translit": "ُbِsْkَt", "root": "كسب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كُلُّ", "translit": "ُّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَفْسٍ", "translit": "ٍsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَسَيَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَyَsَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْكُفَّٰرُ", "translit": "ُrَّٰfُkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لِمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "عُقْبَى", "translit": "àَbْqُʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلدَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّdlٱ", "root": "دور"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "وَيَقُولُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَسْتَ مُرْسَلًاۚ قُلْ كَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ شَهِيدًۢا بَيْنِى وَبَيْنَكُمْ وَمَنْ عِندَهُۥ عِلْمُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ", "translation": "And those who have disbelieved say, \"You are not a messenger.\" Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Sufficient is Allāh as Witness between me and you, and [the witness of] whoever has knowledge of the Scripture.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَسْتَ", "translit": "َtْsَl", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُرْسَلًا", "translit": "āًlَsْrُm", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَفَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَfَk", "root": "كفي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "شَهِيدًۢا", "translit": "āًۢdyِhَhs", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَيْنِى", "translit": "àِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عِندَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عِلْمُ", "translit": "ُmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "ثم انظر كيف أحكم جوانب الأرض بالجبال الراسيات الشوامخ الصم الصلاب وكيف أودع المياه تحتها ففجر العيون وأسأل الأنهار تجرى على وجهها وأخرج من الحجارة اليابسة ومن التراب الكدر ماء رقيقا عذبا صافيا زلالا وجعل به كل شىء حى فأخرج به فنون الأشجار والنبات من حب وعنب وقضب وزيتون ونخل ورمان وفواكه كثيرة لا تحصى مختلفة الأشكال والألوان والطعوم والصفات والأرابيح يفضل بعضها على بعض فى الأكل تسقى بماء واحد وتخرج من أرض واحدة فإن قلت إن اختلافها باختلاف بذورها وأصولها فمتى كان فى النواة نخلة مطوقة لعناقيد الرطب", "english": "Then look at how He has firmly established the sides of the earth with the towering, lofty, solid, and hard mountains, and how He has deposited waters beneath it, so He gushed forth springs and made rivers flow upon its surface, and brought forth from the dry stones and from the turbid soil a delicate, sweet, pure, and clear water, and made with it every living thing alive, so He brought forth with it varieties of trees and plants from grains and grapes and herbs and olives and date palms and pomegranates and many fruits that cannot be enumerated, differing in shapes and colors and tastes and attributes and fragrances, He favors some of them over others in eating, they are watered with one water and come forth from one land. If you say that their difference is due to the difference in their seeds and origins, then when was there in the seed a date palm encircled with clusters of fresh dates, and when was there in a single grain ears of wheat, in each ear one hundred? Then look at the land of the deserts and search its surface and interior, and you will see it as similar soil; when water is sent down upon it, it quivers and swells and brings forth from every delightful pair different colors and plants similar and dissimilar, each one having a taste and fragrance and color and shape that differs from the other. So look at their abundance and the difference in their kinds and the multitude of their forms, then the difference in the natures of plants and the multitude of their benefits, and how Allah the Exalted has deposited strange beneficial medicines: this plant nourishes, and this strengthens, and this gives life, and this kills, and this cools, and this heats, and this when it reaches the stomach suppresses the yellow bile from the depths of the veins, and this transforms into yellow bile, and this suppresses the phlegm and the black bile, and this transforms into them, and this purifies the blood, and this dissolves blood, and this gladdens, and this induces sleep, and this strengthens, and this weakens. Not a leaf nor a blade of grass sprouts from the earth except that in it are benefits that humans are not capable of comprehending their essence, and each one of these plants requires the farmer in its cultivation a specific action: the date palms favor generosity, it is cleared, and the crops are cleared from it of weeds and thickets, and some of that.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k09.doc.txt", "book_title": "Contemplation", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Contemplation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "5": [{"arabic": "وإلهكم إله واحد لا إله إلا هو الرحمن الرحيم إن في خلق السموات والأرض إلى آخر الآية وقل هو الله أحد خمس عشرة مرة ثم يركع ويسجد فإذا قام في الركعة الثانية قرأ فاتحة الكتاب وآية الكرسي وآيتين بعدها إلى قوله أولئك أصحاب النار هم فيها خالدون", "english": "And your God is One God, there is no god but He, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth to the end of the verse, and say 'He is Allah, the One' fifteen times, then bow and prostrate. When he stands for the second unit (Rak'ah), he recites the Opening (Al-Fatihah) of the Book and the Throne Verse (Ayat al-Kursi) and two verses after it up to His saying 'Those are the companions of the Fire; they will abide therein eternally.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "6": [{"arabic": "[13] حديث إن النبي ﷺ لم يزل يسأل في أمته حتى قيل له أما ترضى وقد أنزل عليك وإن ربك لذو مغفرة للناس على ظلمهم لم أجده بهذا اللفظ وروى ابن أبي حاتم والثعلبي في تفسيرهما من رواية علي بن زيد بن جدعان عن سعيد بن المسيب قال لما نزلت هذه الآية قال رسول الله ﷺ لولا عفو الله وتجاوزه ما هنأ أحد العيش الحديث.", "english": "Hadith: Indeed, the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not cease asking for his nation until it was said to him: 'Are you not satisfied? And has been revealed to you: \"And indeed, your Lord is the Possessor (Dhu) of forgiveness for the people upon their wrongdoing.\"' I did not find it with this wording. And Ibn Abi Hatim and Al-Tha'labi narrated in their two interpretations (Tafsir) from the narration of Ali bin Zaid bin Jad'an from Sa'id bin Al-Musayyib who said: When this verse was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'Were it not for the pardon (Afw) of Allah and His overlooking (Tajawuz), no one would enjoy life.' The hadith.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book3.doc.txt", "book_title": "Fear and Hope", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Fear and Hope'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "وقال تعالى: ﴿ وإن ربك لذوا مغفرة للناس على ظلمهم ﴾ {} ويقال: (إن النبي ﭬ لم يزل يسأل في أمته حتى قيل له أما ترضى وقد أنزلت عليك هذه الآية: ﴿ وإن ربك لذو مغفرة للناس ظلمهم ﴾ {}[13])", "english": "And He, the Exalted, said: 'And indeed your Lord is possessor of forgiveness for the people upon their wrongdoing' {Quran 13:6}. And it is said: (Indeed the Prophet ﷺ did not cease asking for his nation until it was said to him: Are you not satisfied when this verse has been revealed to you: 'And indeed your Lord is possessor of forgiveness for the people upon their wrongdoing' {Quran 13:6}[13]).", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book3.doc.txt", "book_title": "Fear and Hope", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Fear and Hope'", "badge": "General"}], "8": [{"arabic": "بل ما قدره الله تعالى من إقبال ونعمة فلا بد أن يدوم إلى أجل غير معلوم قدره الله سبحانه. فلا حيلة في دفعه، بل كل شيء عنده بمقدار، ولكل أجل كتاب.", "english": "Rather, what Allah the Exalted has decreed of favor and blessing must necessarily last until an unknown term that Allah the Glorified has determined. There is no means to repel it, rather everything with Him is by measure, and for every term there is a book.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book5a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "11": [{"arabic": "\nمخلوقاته تباركت وتعاليت سبحانك سبحانك يا حي يا قيوم يا عليم يا  حليم  سبحانك\nلا إله إلا أنت وحدك لا شريك لك تحيي وتميت وأنت حي لا تموت  بيدك  الخير  وأنت\nعلى كل شيء قدير.\n  (الباب الرابع في أدعية مأثورة عن النبي ﭬ  وعن أصحابه رضي الله عنهم محذوفة\n  الأسانيد منتخبة من جملة ما جمعه أبو طالب المكي وابن خزيمة وابن منذر رحمهم\n                                    الله)\n   يستحب للمريد إذا أصبح أن يكون أحب أوراده الدعاء كما سيأتي ذكره  في  كتاب\nالأوراد فإن كنت من المريدين لحرث الآخرة المقتدين برسول الل", "english": "[140] Hadith: 'O Allah, I ask You for well-being in my religion, my worldly life, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, cover my private parts, secure my fears, reduce my stumbles, and protect me from in front of me and from behind me and from my right and from my left and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being taken from below me.' Reported by Abu Dawud, al-Nasa'i, Ibn Majah, and al-Hakim from the narration of Ibn 'Umar, who said: 'The Prophet (peace be upon him) would not leave these words when evening and morning came.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance", "badge": "Du'a"}], "13": [{"arabic": "وإذا سمعت صوت الرعد فقل سبحان من يسبح الرعد بحمده والملائكة من خيفته[207] فإن رأيت الصواعق فقل اللهم لا تقتلنا بغضبك ولا تهلكنا بعذابك وعافنا قبل ذلك[208]", "english": "And if you hear the sound of thunder, say: 'Glory be to the One whom the thunder glorifies with His praise and the angels from fear of Him.' [207] Then if you see the lightning bolts, say: 'O Allah, do not kill us with Your anger and do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that.' [208]", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "[207]  حديث القول إذا سمع صوت الرعد سبحان من يسبح الرعد بحمده والملائكة من خيفته أخرجه مالك في الموطأ عن عبد الله بن الزبير موقوفا ولم أجده مرفوعا.", "english": "[207] The saying when hearing the sound of thunder: 'Glory be to the One whom the thunder glorifies with His praise and the angels from fear of Him.' It was reported by Malik in Al-Muwatta' from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr as a statement of a companion (Mawquf) and I did not find it as a prophetic tradition (Marfu').", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication", "badge": "Hadith"}], "15": [{"arabic": "وهذا الورد من أطول الأوراد وأمتعها للعباد وهو أحد والآصال التي ذكرها الله تعالى إذ قال: ﴿ ولله يسجد من في السموات والأرض طوعا وكرها وظلالهم بالغدو والآصال ﴾ {} وإذا سجد لله عز وجل الجمادات فكيف يجوز أن يغفل العبد العاقل عن أنواع العبادات.", "english": "And this spiritual practice (Wird) is among the longest spiritual practices and most delightful for the worshippers, and it is one of the evening times (Al-Asal) that Allah the Exalted mentioned when He said: 'And to Allah prostrates whoever is in the heavens and the earth, willingly and unwillingly, and their shadows [as well] in the mornings and the evenings (Al-Ghuduww wal-Asal).' {} And if the inanimate objects prostrate to Allah the Mighty and Majestic, then how can it be permissible for the rational servant (Al-Abd al-Aqil) to be heedless of the various types of acts of worship (Ibadat).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فلو لم يكن بين يدي الموتي إلا هول تلك النفخة لكان ذلك جديرا بأن يتقى فإنها نفخة وصيحة يصعق بها من فى السموات والأرض يعنى يموتون بها إلا من شاء الله وهو بعض الملائكة ولذلك قال رسول الله ﭬ: (كيف أنعم وصاحب الصور قد التقم القرن وحنى الجبهة وأصغى بالأذن متى يؤمر فينفخ[144]) قال مقاتل: الصور هو القرن وذلك أن إسرافيل عليه السلام واضع فاه على القرن كهيئة البوق ودائرة رأس القرن كعرض السموات والأرض وهو شاخص بصره نحو العرش ينتظر متى يؤمر فينفخ النفخة الأولى فإذا نفخ صعق من فى السموات والأرض أى مات كل حيوا", "english": "If there were nothing before the dead except the terror of that blowing (of the Trumpet), it would be worthy of being feared, for it is a blowing and a cry by which those in the heavens and the earth are struck unconscious, meaning they die by it except whom Allah wills, and that is some of the angels. And for that reason, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'How can I enjoy comfort when the possessor of the Trumpet has taken the horn into his mouth, lowered his forehead, and inclined his ear, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow?' [144] Muqatil said: The Trumpet (As-Sur) is the horn, and that is because Israfil (upon him be peace) has placed his mouth on the horn like the form of a trumpet, and the circle of the horn's head is like the expanse of the heavens and the earth, and he is fixing his gaze toward the Throne, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow the first blowing. And when he blows, those in the heavens and the earth are struck unconscious, meaning every living creature dies from the intensity of the terror except whom Allah wills, and that is Jibril, Mika'il, Israfil, and the Angel of Death (Malak al-Mawt). Then the Angel of Death is commanded to take the spirit (Ruh) of Jibril, then the spirit (Ruh) of Mika'il, then the spirit (Ruh) of Israfil, then the Angel of Death is commanded and he dies. Then the creation remains after the first blowing in the Intermediate State (Al-Barzakh) for forty years. Then Allah the Exalted revives Israfil and commands him to blow the second blowing, and that is His saying, the Exalted: 'Then it will be blown into it another time, and behold, they are standing, looking.' [Quran 39:68] On their feet, looking at the Resurrection. And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'When I was sent, I was sent to the possessor of the Trumpet, and he inclined it to his mouth, and advanced one foot and delayed another, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow. Indeed, fear the blowing!' [145] So reflect upon the creation and their humiliation, their breaking, and their submission at the time of being raised up, out of fear of this unconsciousness and waiting for it.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "16": [{"arabic": "وإن صدقوك فى مودتهم إياك فلا يملكون لك ولا لأنفسهم نفعا ولا ضرا ولا موتا ولا حياة ولا نشورا وقد يكون فى بلدك من أغنياء اليهود والنصارى من يزيد جاهه على جاهك وقد اشتغلت بهذا الغرور وغفلت عن النظر فى جمال ملكوت السموات والأرض ثم غفلت عن التنعم بالنظر إلى جلال مالك الملكوت والملك وما مثلك ومثل عقلك إلا مثل النملة تخرج من جحرها الذى حفرته فى قصر مشيد من قصور الملك رفيع البنيان حصين الأركان مزين بالجوارى والغلمان وأنواع الذخائر والنفائس فإنها إذا خرجت من جحرها ولقيت صاحبتها لم تتحدث لو قدرت على النطق", "english": "And if they are truthful in their affection for you, they do not possess for you nor for themselves benefit (Nafʿ) nor harm (Ḍarr), nor death nor life nor resurrection. And there may be in your land among the wealthy Jews and Christians one whose status (Jāh) exceeds your status, and you have busied yourself with this delusion and neglected contemplating the beauty of the dominion (Mulkūt) of the heavens and the earth, then neglected enjoying the contemplation of the majesty of the Owner of the dominion (Mulkūt) and the kingdom (Mulk). And your likeness and the likeness of your intellect (ʿAql) is only like the ant that emerges from its hole which it dug in a constructed palace among the palaces of the king, lofty in structure, fortified in foundations, adorned with maidens and youths, and types of treasures and precious things. For when it emerges from its hole and meets its companion, it would not converse, if it had the capability of speech, except about its house and its sustenance and the manner of its storage. As for the condition of the palace and the king who is in the palace, it is remote from it and from reflecting upon it; rather, it has no capability to transcend in contemplation beyond itself, its sustenance, and its house to other than it. And just as the ant neglected the palace and its ground, its roof, its walls, and all its structure, and neglected also its inhabitants, so you too are neglectful of the House of Allah, the Exalted, and of His angels who are the inhabitants of its abode. So you do not know of the heaven except what the ant knows of the roof of your house, and you do not know of the angels of the heavens except what the ant knows of you and the inhabitants of your house. Indeed, there is no way for the ant to know you and know the wonders of your palace and the marvels of the Maker's craftsmanship in it. But as for you, you have the capability to know your Lord and contemplate His majesty and reflect upon the wonders of His dominion. So look at the heaven and the earth and say: 'Who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth?' Say: 'Allah.' Say: 'Have you then taken besides Him protectors who possess not for themselves benefit (Nafʿ) nor harm (Ḍarr)?' Say: 'Are the blind and the seeing equal? Or are the darknesses and the light equal? Or have they made for Allah partners who created like His creation, so the creation seemed alike to them?' Say: 'Allah is the Creator of all things, and He is the One, the Subduer (Al-Qahhār).'", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k09.doc.txt", "book_title": "Contemplation", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Contemplation'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "17": [{"arabic": "وأما المدرك بالشرع فهو أن يكون إجراؤه على الظاهر ممكنا ولكنه يروى أنه أريد به غير الظاهر كما ورد في تفسير قوله تعالى: ﴿ أنزل من السماء ماء فسالت أودية بقدرها فاحتمل السيل زبدا رابيا ۚ ومما يوقدون عليه في النار ابتغاء حلية أو متاع زبد مثله ۚ كذلك يضرب الله الحق والباطل ۚ فأما الزبد فيذهب جفاء ۖ وأما ما ينفع الناس فيمكث في الأرض ۚ كذلك يضرب الله الأمثال ﴾ وأن معنى الماء ههنا هو القرآن ومعنى الأودية هي القلوب وأن بعضها احتملت شيئا كثيرا وبعضها قليلا وبعضها لم يحتمل والزبد مثل الكفر والنفاق فإنه وإن", "english": "As for what is perceived through the Sharia (Islamic law), it is that applying it according to its apparent meaning is possible, but it is narrated that something other than the apparent meaning was intended, as has come in the interpretation of His saying, the Exalted: 'He sends down from the sky water, so the valleys flow according to their measure, and the flood carries a rising foam. And from that which they kindle in the fire, desiring ornament or utility, is a foam like it. Thus does Allah strike truth and falsehood. As for the foam, it vanishes, [being] cast off; but as for that which benefits the people, it remains on the earth. Thus does Allah strike the similitudes.' And that the meaning of the water here is the Quran, and the meaning of the valleys are the Hearts (Qulub), and that some of them carried much, some little, and some did not carry at all, and the foam is like disbelief (Kufr) and hypocrisy (Nifaq), for even if it appears and floats on the surface of the water, it does not remain, and the guidance (Hidayah) that benefits the people remains.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "19": [{"arabic": "وقال تعالى ﴿ إنما يتذكر أولوا الألباب ﴾ {} فالذي آثر غرور الدنيا على نعيم الآخرة فليس من ذوي الألباب ولذلك لا تنكشف له أسرار الكتاب.", "english": "And the Exalted said: 'Only those possessing intellects (أولوا الألباب) remember (يتذكر).' So the one who prefers the deception (غرور) of this world over the bliss (نعيم) of the Hereafter is not among those possessing intellects (ذوي الألباب), and therefore the secrets (أسرار) of the Book do not become unveiled to him.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "22": [{"arabic": "الوظيفة الرابعة: أن يظهر حيث يعلم أن في إظهاره ترغيبا للناس في الاقتداء ويحرس سره من داعية الرياء بالطريق الذي سنذكره في معالجة الرياء في كتاب الرياء فقد قال الله عز وجل: ﴿ إن تبدوا الصدقات فنعما هي ﴾ {} وذلك حيث يقتضي الحال الإبداء إما للاقتداء وإما لأن السائل إنما سأل على ملأ من الناس فلا ينبغي أن يترك التصدق خيفة من الرياء في الإظهار بل ينبغي أن يتصدق ويحفظ سره عن الرياء بقدر الإمكان وهذا لأن في الإظهار محذورا ثالثا سوى المن والرياء وهو هتك ستر الفقير فإنه ربما يتأذى بأن يرى في صورة المحتاج ف", "english": "The fourth duty: That he makes it public where he knows that in its public display there is encouragement for people to follow his example, and he guards his secret from the prompting of showing off (Riya') through the method that we will mention in treating showing off (Riya') in the Book of Showing Off (Riya'). For Allah the Exalted has said: 'If you disclose your charitable expenditures, they are good' (Quran 2:271). This is where the situation necessitates disclosure, either for emulation or because the asker asked publicly among people. So one should not refrain from giving charity out of fear of showing off (Riya') in public display; rather, one should give charity and guard his secret from showing off (Riya') as much as possible. This is because in public display there is a third danger besides reminding of favor (Al-Mann) and showing off (Riya'), which is exposing the cover of the poor person. For perhaps he is harmed by being seen in the image of the needy. So whoever makes the request public is the one who exposed his own cover. Therefore, one should not be cautious of this meaning in his public display, and it is like exposing immorality upon one who concealed it, for that is prohibited, and spying into it and habitual mention of it is forbidden. As for whoever exposes it, establishing the punishment upon him is publicizing, but he is the cause in it. And with a meaning like this, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Whoever casts off the garment of modesty (Al-Haya'), then there is no backbiting for him.' And Allah the Exalted has said: 'And spend from what We have provided for you secretly and publicly' (Quran 13:22). He encouraged to public display also because of the benefit of encouragement in it. So let the servant (Al-'Abd) be precise in contemplation in weighing this benefit against the danger that is in it, for that differs according to circumstances and persons. Indeed, public announcement in some circumstances for some persons may be better. And whoever knows the benefits and dangers and does not look with the eye of desire (Al-Shahwah), the most appropriate and fitting for every situation becomes clear to him.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Zakat", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Mysteries of Zakat'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "25": [{"arabic": "ي الله عنه: ثلاث بهن ينهدم الزمان إحداهن زلة العالم. وقال ابن مسعود: سيأتي على الناس زمان تملح فيه عذوبة القلوب فلا ينتفع بالعلم يومئذ عالمه ولا متعلمه فتكون قلوب علمائهم مثل السباخ من ذوات الملح ينزل عليها قطر السماء فلا يوجد لها عذوبة وذلك إذا مالت قلوب العلماء إلى حب الدنيا وإيثارها على الآخرة فعند ذلك يسلبها الله تعالى ينابيع الحكمة ويطفىء مصابيح الهدى من قلوبهم فيخبرك عالمهم حين تلقاه أنه يخشى الله بلسانه والفجور ظاهر في عمله فما أخصب الألسن يومئذ وما أجدب القلوب فوالله الذي لا إله إلا هو م", "english": "In the name of God, about him: three things by which time is destroyed, one of them is the slip of the scholar. And Ibn Mas'ud said: There will come upon people a time when the sweetness of the hearts (Qulub) becomes salty, so neither its scholar nor its learner benefits from knowledge on that day, so the hearts (Qulub) of their scholars become like the salty lands, rain falls upon them but no sweetness is found for them, and that is when the hearts (Qulub) of the scholars incline to the love of the worldly life (Dunya) and prefer it over the Hereafter (Akhirah), then at that time God Almighty strips them of the springs of wisdom and extinguishes the lamps of guidance from their hearts (Qulub), so their scholar informs you when you meet him that he fears God with his tongue while corruption is apparent in his action, so how fertile are the tongues on that day and how barren are the hearts (Qulub)! By God, there is no god but Him, that is only because the teachers taught for other than God Almighty and the learners learned for other than God Almighty. And in the Torah and the Gospel it is written: Do not seek knowledge of what you do not know until you act upon what you know. And Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: You are in a time where whoever leaves a tenth of what he knows is destroyed, and there will come a time where whoever acts upon a tenth of what he knows is saved, and that is due to the abundance of the idle. And know that the likeness of the scholar is like the judge, and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ((Judges are three: a judge who judges with truth while knowing it, so that one is in Paradise; and a judge who judges with injustice while knowing it or not knowing it, so he is in Hell; and a judge who judges with other than what God has commanded, so he is in Hell))[161]. And Ka'b, may God have mercy on him, said: There will be in the end of time scholars who urge people to asceticism (Zuhd) in the worldly life (Dunya) but do not practice asceticism (Zuhd) themselves, and who frighten people but do not fear themselves, and who forbid visiting the rulers but come to them, and who prefer the worldly life (Dunya) over the Hereafter (Akhirah), they eat with their tongues, they draw near the rich to the exclusion of the poor, they become jealous over knowledge as women become jealous over men, one of them becomes angry at his companion if he sits with another, those are the tyrants, enemies of the Most Merciful. And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ((Indeed, Satan sometimes delays you with knowledge, so it was said: O Messenger of God, and how is that? He said, peace and blessings be upon him: He says seek knowledge and do not act until you know, so knowledge remains saying and action remains delayed until he dies and has not acted))[162]. And Sari al-Saqati said: A man secluded himself for worship, he was eager to seek the outward knowledge (Ilm al-Zahir), so I asked him and he said: I saw in a dream a speaker saying to me: How long will you waste knowledge? May God waste you! So I said: Indeed, I memorize it. He said: The preservation of knowledge is acting upon it, so I left the seeking and turned to the action. And Ibn Mas'ud, may God be pleased with him, said: Knowledge is not with abundant narration, indeed knowledge is fear (Khashyah). And al-Hasan said: Learn whatever you wish to learn, for by God, God will not reward you until you act, for the foolish ones, their concern is narration, and the scholars, their concern is care (Ri'ayah). And Malik, may God have mercy on him, said:", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "وكيف لا يبغض وهو لا ينفك عن الكذب والغيبة والغدر والخيانة والغل والحسد والنفاق والإفساد بين الناس والخديعة وهو ممن يسعون في قطع ما أمر الله به أن يوصل ويفسدون في الأرض؟ وقال تعالى \"إنما السبيل على الذين يظلمون الناس ويبغون في الأرض بغير الحق\" والنمام منهم. وقال ﭬ \"إن من شرار الناس من اتقاه الناس لشره\"[236] والنمام منهم. وقال \"لا يدخل الجنة قاطع\" قيل وما القاطع؟ قال \"قاطع بين الناس\"[237] وهو النمام وقيل قاطع الرحم.", "english": "And how should he not be hated when he does not desist from lying, backbiting (Ghibah), treachery, betrayal, malice, envy, hypocrisy, corruption between people, and deception? And he is among those who strive to cut off what Allah has commanded to be connected and who spread corruption in the earth? And Allah the Exalted said: \"Indeed, the way is only against those who wrong the people and tyrannize upon the earth without right\" and the slanderer (Nammam) is among them. And He said: \"Indeed, among the worst of people is he whom people fear for his evil\" and the slanderer is among them. And He said: \"The cutter will not enter Paradise.\" It was said: \"And what is the cutter?\" He said: \"The one who cuts between people\" and he is the slanderer, and it is said: the one who cuts kinship ties.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book4a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Anger and Hatred", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Anger and Hatred'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "26": [{"arabic": "فهذه إحدى المباحات ووراءها آفات عظيمة أعظم من هذه، وهو أن النفس تفرح بالتنعم في الدنيا وتركن إليها وتطمئن إليها أشراً وبطراً حتى تصير ثملة كالسكران الذي لا يفيق من سكره. وذلك الفرح بالدنيا سم قاتل يسري في العروق فيخرج من القلب الخوف والحزن وذكر الموت وأهوال يوم القيامة، وهذا هو موت القلب. قال الله تعالى \"ورضوا بالحياة الدنيا واطمأنوابها\" وقال تعالى \"وما الحياة الدنيا في الآخرة إلا متاع\" وقال تعالى \"اعلموا إنما الحياة الدنيا لعب ولهو وزينة وتفاخر بينكم وتكاثر في الأموال والأولاد\" وكل ذلك ذم لها ف", "english": "This is one of the permissible things, and behind it are great calamities greater than this, which is that the Soul (Nafs) rejoices in indulgence in the worldly life and leans towards it and becomes content with it in arrogance and pride until it becomes intoxicated like a drunkard who does not recover from his drunkenness. And that rejoicing in the worldly life is a deadly poison that flows through the veins and removes from the Heart (Qalb) the fear and grief and remembrance (Dhikr) of death and the terrors of the Day of Resurrection, and this is the death of the Heart (Qalb). Allah the Exalted said: 'And they were pleased with the worldly life and became content with it' and He the Exalted said: 'And what is the worldly life in the Hereafter except enjoyment' and He the Exalted said: 'Know that the worldly life is only play and amusement and adornment and boasting among you and increase in wealth and children' and all of that is censure of it, so we ask Allah for safety.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book2a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "28": [{"arabic": "فنقول الوجد الحق هو ما ينشأ من فرط حب الله تعالى وصدق إرادته والشوق إلى لقائه وذلك يهيج بسماع القرآن أيضا وإنما الذي لا يهيج بسماع القرآن حب الخلق وعشق المخلوق ويدل على ذلك قوله تعالى ألا بذكر الله تطمئن القلوب وقوله تعالى مثاني تقشعر منه جلود الذين يخشون ربهم ثم تلين جلودهم وقلوبهم إلى ذكر الله وكل ما يوجد عقيب السماع في النفس فهو وجد فالطمأنينة والاقشعرار والخشية ولين القلب كل ذلك وجد وقد قال الله تعالى إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم وقال تعالى لو أنزلنا هذا القرآن على جبل لرأيته", "english": "We say: The true spiritual state (Wajd) is what arises from excessive love (Hubb) of Allah the Exalted and the sincerity of one's intention (Iradah) and longing (Shawq) for meeting Him, and that is also stirred by hearing the Quran. Indeed, what is not stirred by hearing the Quran is love (Hubb) of creation and infatuation (Ishaq) with the created. Evidence for this is His statement, the Exalted: 'Is it not by the Remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah that the Hearts (Qulub) find tranquility?' and His statement, the Exalted: 'Verses repeated, from which the skins of those who fear their Lord shiver, then their skins and their Hearts (Qulub) soften to the Remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah.' And everything that occurs in the Soul (Nafs) following hearing is a spiritual state (Wajd). So tranquility (Tuma'ninah), shivering (Iqsha'rar), fear (Khashyah), and softening of the Heart (Qalb) - all of that is a spiritual state (Wajd). And Allah the Exalted has said: 'Indeed, the believers are those whose Hearts (Qulub) tremble when Allah is mentioned.' And He the Exalted said: 'If We had sent down this Quran upon a mountain, you would have seen it humbled, split asunder from the fear (Khashyah) of Allah.' So trembling (Wajal) and humility (Khushu') are spiritual states (Wajd) from the category of conditions (Ahwal), even if they are not from the category of unveilings (Mukashafat), but they may become a cause for unveilings (Mukashafat) and awakenings (Tanbihat).", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Audition and Ecstasy", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Audition and Ecstasy'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وهذا القلب هو الذي يستقر فيه الذكر  قال  الله  تعالى  ألا  بذكر  الله  تطمئن القلوب وأما الآثار المذمومة فإنها مثل دخان مظلم يتصاعد إلى  مرآة  القلب  ولا يزال يتراكم عليه مرة بعد أخرى إلى أن يسود  ويظلم  ويصير  بالكلية  محجوبا  عن الله تعالى وهو الطبع وهو الرين", "english": "And this Heart (Qalb) is that in which the Remembrance (Dhikr) settles. Allah the Exalted said: 'Is it not by the Remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah that the Hearts (Qulub) find tranquility?' And as for the blameworthy effects, they are like dark smoke ascending to the mirror of the Heart (Qalb) and it continues to accumulate upon it time after time until it blackens and darkens and becomes completely veiled from Allah the Exalted, and that is the sealing (Tab') and that is the rust (Rayn).", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وقال قتادة في قوله تعالى: \"الذين آمنوا وتطمئن قلوبهم بذكر الله ألا بذكر الله تطمئن القلوب\" قال: هشت إليه واستأنست به.", "english": "And Qatada said regarding His saying, the Exalted: \"Those who have believed and whose hearts find rest (Tatma'innu) in the remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah. Unquestionably, by the remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah hearts find rest (Tatma'innu).\" He said: They became joyful (Hashat) towards Him and found intimacy (Ista'ansat) with Him.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وهو القلب الذي أقبل الله عز وجل بوجهه عليه وهو القلب المطمئن المراد بقوله تعالى ألا بذكر الله تطمئن القلوب وبقوله عز وجل يا أيتها النفس المطمئنة", "english": "And it is the Heart (Qalb) upon which Allah the Exalted has turned His face, and it is the tranquil heart intended by His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, by the Remembrance (Dhikr) of Allah do hearts find tranquility' and by His saying, the Exalted: 'O tranquil Soul (Nafs)'.", "book_file": "vol3_j3-k01.doc.txt", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}], "31": [{"arabic": "الأصل الثالث: أن فعل العبد وإن كان كسبا للعبد فلا يخرج عن كونه مرادا لله سبحانه فلا يجري في الملك والملكوت طرفة عين ولا لفتة خاطر ولا فلتة ناظر إلا بقضاء الله وقدرته وبإرادته ومشيئته ومنه الشر والخير والنفع والضر والإسلام والكفر والعرفان والنكر والفوز والخسران والغواية والرشد والطاعة والعصيان والشرك والإيمان لا راد لقضائه ولا معقب لحكمه يضل من يشاء ويهدي من يشاء لا يسئل عما يفعل وهم يسألون ويدل عليه من النقل قول الأمة قاطبة ما شاء كان وما لم يشأ لم يكن وقول الله عز وجل أن لو يشاء الله لهدى الناس", "english": "The third foundation: That the action of the servant, even if it is an acquisition (kasb) for the servant, does not depart from being willed by Allah, glorified be He. Not a blink of an eye, nor a turn of thought, nor a glance of sight occurs in the dominion (mulk) and the kingdom (malakut) except by the decree (qada) of Allah and His power (qudrah) and by His will (iradah) and His volition (mashiyyah). From it are evil and good, benefit and harm, Islam and disbelief (kufr), recognition (irfan) and denial (nukr), success (fawz) and loss (khusran), misguidance (ghawayah) and guidance (rushd), obedience (ta'ah) and disobedience (asiyan), polytheism (shirk) and faith (iman). There is no repeller of His decree and no reverser of His judgment. He misguides whom He wills and guides whom He wills. He is not questioned about what He does, while they will be questioned. What indicates this from transmission is the saying of the entire community: 'What He wills is, and what He does not will is not,' and the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: 'If Allah had willed, He would have guided all people together' (Quran 13:31), and His saying, exalted be He: 'And if We had willed, We could have given every soul its guidance' (Quran 32:13). What indicates it from the aspect of intellect is that sins (ma'asi) and crimes (jaraim), if Allah dislikes them and does not will them, yet they occur in accordance with the will of the enemy, Iblis, may Allah curse him, even though he is an enemy to Allah, glorified be He, and what occurs in accordance with the will of the enemy is more than what occurs in accordance with His will, exalted be He. I wonder how a Muslim permits reducing the dominion of the Compeller (al-Jabbar), Possessor of Majesty (Jalal) and Honor (Ikram), to a rank that if the leadership of a village chief were reduced to it, he would disdain it. For if what continues for the enemy of the chief in the village is more than what is established for him, he would disdain his leadership and disavow his authority. Disobedience (ma'siyah) is predominant over creation, and all of that occurs according to the innovators in opposition to the will of the Truth, exalted be He. This is the utmost weakness and incapacity. Exalted is the Lord of lords above what the wrongdoers say, greatly exalted. Then, whenever it becomes clear that the actions of the servants are created by Allah, it is correct that they are willed by Him. If it is said: 'How does He forbid what He wills and command what He does not will?' We say: Command (amr) is different from will (iradah). Therefore, when a master strikes his servant and the ruler reproaches him for it, and he excuses himself by the rebellion of his servant against him, and the ruler disbelieves him, so he wants to manifest his proof by commanding the servant to do an action and he disobeys him in the presence of the ruler, so he says to him: 'Saddle this mount in the sight of the ruler.' Thus, he commands him to what he does not want compliance with, even if he were not a commander.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Insight"}], "33": [{"arabic": "النظر الثاني نظر من لم يبلغ الى مقام الفناء عن نفسه وهؤلاء قسمان قسم لم يثبتوا الا وجود انفسهم وانكروا ان يكون لهم رب يعبد وهؤلاء هم العميان المنكوسون وعماهم في كلتا العينين لأنهم نفوا ما هو الثابت تحقيقا وهو القيوم الذي هو قائم بنفسه وقائم على كل نفس بما كسبت وكل قائم فقائم به ولم يقتصروا على هذا حتى اثبتوا انفسهم ولو عرفوا لعلموا انهم من حيث هم هم لا ثبات لهم ولا وجود لهم وانما وجودهم من حيث أوجدوا لا من حيث وجدوا وفرق بين الموجود وبين الموجد وليس في الوجود الا موجود واحد وموجد فالموجود حق وال", "english": "The second perspective is that of those who have not reached the station of annihilation (Fana) from their selves (Nafs), and these are two groups. The first group affirmed nothing but the existence of their own selves (Nafs) and denied that they have a Lord (Rabb) to worship. These are the inverted blind ones, and their blindness is in both eyes because they denied what is truly established, which is the Self-Subsisting (Al-Qayyum) who is self-subsisting (Qa'im) by Himself and standing (Qa'im) over every soul (Nafs) with what it has earned, and every standing (Qa'im) is standing (Qa'im) by Him. They did not limit themselves to this until they affirmed their own selves (Nafs). If they had known, they would have realized that from their own perspective, they have no stability and no existence, and their existence is from the perspective of being brought into existence (Uujidu), not from the perspective of being found (Wujidu). There is a difference between the existent (Mawjud) and the one who brings into existence (Mujid), and in existence (Wujud) there is only one existent (Mawjud) and one who brings into existence (Mujid). The existent (Mawjud) is true, and the one who brings into existence (Mujid) is false from his own perspective. The existent (Mawjud) is standing (Qa'im) and self-subsisting (Qayyum), and the one who brings into existence (Mujid) is perishing and annihilated. And when everything upon it perishes, nothing remains except the Face of your Lord (Rabb), the Possessor of Majesty and Honor.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "أما المعرفة التي تثمر هذه الحالة فهو العلم بأن الله مطلع على الضمائر عالم بالسرائر رقيب على أعمال العباد قائم على كل نفس بما كسبت وأن سر القلب في حقه مكشوف كما أن ظاهر البشرة للخلق مكشوف بل اشد من ذلك فهذه المعرفة إذا صارت يقينا أعنى أنها خلت عن الشك ثم استولت بعد ذلك على القلب قهرته فرب علم لا شك فيه لا يغلب على القلب كالعلم بالموت فإذا استولت على القلب استجرت القلب إلى مراعاة جانب الرقيب وصرفت همه إليه والموقنون بهذه المعرفة هم المقربون وهم ينقسمون إلى الصديقين وإلى أصحاب اليمين فمراقبتهم على ", "english": "As for the knowledge that produces this state, it is the knowledge that Allah is aware of the innermost thoughts, knows the secrets, watches over the deeds of the servants, standing over every soul (Nafs) by what it has earned, and that the secret of the heart (Qalb) is unveiled to Him just as the outward appearance of the skin is unveiled to creation, indeed more than that. This knowledge, when it becomes certainty—meaning it is free from doubt—and then dominates the heart (Qalb), overpowering it—for there is knowledge without doubt that does not dominate the heart (Qalb), like the knowledge of death—when it dominates the heart (Qalb), it draws the heart (Qalb) to observe the side of the Watcher and diverts its concern to Him. Those certain of this knowledge are the ones brought near, and they are divided into the truthful ones (Siddiqin) and the companions of the right hand. Their watchfulness is on two levels: the first level is the watchfulness of the brought near among the truthful ones (Siddiqin), which is the watchfulness of veneration and reverence, meaning that the heart (Qalb) becomes absorbed in observing that majesty and broken under awe, so there remains no room in it for turning to others at all. This watchfulness we do not prolong in detailing its actions, for it is confined to the heart (Qalb). As for the limbs, they cease from turning to the permissible, let alone the forbidden, and when they move with acts of obedience, they are as if used by them, not needing management and stabilization in preserving them on the path of correctness. Rather, the subjects are guided by the one who owns the dog of the shepherd, and the heart (Qalb) is the shepherd. When it becomes absorbed in the Worshipped, the limbs become used, proceeding on correctness and uprightness without effort, and this is the one whose concern has become a single concern, so it suffices him.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monitoring and Accounting", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monitoring and Accounting'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ومن لم يعقله عقله ولا نهاه نهاه عن أن يقول لساني حادث ولكن ما يحدث فيه بقدرتي الحادثة قديم فاقطع عن عقله طمعك وكف عن خطابه لسانك ومن لم يفهم أن القديم عبارة عما ليس قبله شيء وأن الباء قبل السين في قولك بسم الله فلا يكون السين المتأخر عن الباء قديما فنزه عن الالتفات إليه قلبك فلله سبحانه سر في إبعاد بعض العباد ومن يضلل الله فما له من هاد ومن استبعد أن يسمع موسى عليه السلام في الدنيا كلاما ليس بصوت ولا حرف فليستنكر أن يرى في الآخرة موجودا ليس بجسم ولا لون وإن عقل أن يرى ما ليس بلون ولا جسم ولا قدر", "english": "And whoever his intellect does not comprehend it, and his intellect does not forbid him from saying: 'My tongue is created (hadith), but what occurs in it by my created power is eternal (qadim),' then cut off hope from his intellect and restrain your tongue from addressing him. And whoever does not understand that 'the Eternal (al-Qadim)' is an expression for what has nothing before it, and that the 'ba' comes before the 'sin' in your saying 'Bismillah,' so the 'sin' that follows the 'ba' cannot be eternal, then purify your heart (qalb) from paying attention to him. For Allah, glorified be He, has a secret (sirr) in distancing some of the servants, and 'whom Allah misguides, for him there is no guide (had).' And whoever finds it far-fetched that Moses, peace be upon him, heard in this world speech (kalam) that is not sound nor letter, let him find it strange to see in the Hereafter an existent that is not body nor color. And if he comprehends that he sees what has no color, body, measure, nor quantity, and he has not yet seen other than it, then let him comprehend in the sense of hearing what he comprehended in the sense of sight. And if he comprehends that He has one knowledge (ilm) that is knowledge of all existents, then let him comprehend one attribute (sifah) of the Essence (dhat) that is speech (kalam) of all that is indicated by expressions. And if he comprehends the existence of the seven heavens and the existence of Paradise (Jannah) and Hellfire (Nar) written on a small paper and preserved in the measure of an atom (dharrah) of the heart (qalb), and that all of that is visible in the measure of a lens of the pupil without the essence (dhat) of the heavens, earth, Paradise, and Hellfire residing in the pupil, heart, and paper, then let him comprehend the existence of the speech (kalam) being recited by tongues, preserved in hearts (qulub), written in copies of the Quran (masahif) without the essence (dhat) of the speech residing in them. For if the essence (dhat) of the speech by the Book of Allah resided in the paper, then the essence (dhat) of Allah, exalted be He, would reside by writing His name in the paper, and the essence (dhat) of the Hellfire would reside by writing its name in the paper, and it would burn.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "وَلنذكر  فضيلة  المراقبة  ثم  درجاتها  أما  الفضيلة  فقد  سأل  جبريل  عليه  السلام  عن  الإحسان  فقال  أن  تعبد  الله  كأنك  تراه  حديث  متفق  عليه  من  حديث  أبى  هريرة  ورواه  مسلم  من  حديث  عمر  وقد  تقدم  وقال  عليه  السلام  أعبد  الله  كأنك  تراه  فإن  لم  تكن  تراه  فإنه  يراك  حديث  اعبد  الله  كأنك  تراه  الحديث  تقدم  وقد  قال  تعالى  أفمن  هو  قائم  على  كل  نفس  بما  كسبت  وقال  تعالى  ألم  يعلم  بأن  الله  يرى  وقال  الله  تعالى  إن  الله  كان  عليكم  رقيبا  وقال  تعالى  والذين  هم ", "english": "And let us mention the virtue (Fadilah) of vigilance (Muraqabah) then its degrees. As for the virtue, Jibril (Gabriel), peace be upon him, asked about excellence (Ihsan), and he said: 'That you worship Allah as if you see Him' - a hadith agreed upon from the narration of Abu Hurairah, and Muslim narrated it from the narration of Umar, and it has preceded. And he, peace be upon him, said: 'Worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, indeed He sees you' - the hadith 'Worship Allah as if you see Him' has preceded. And Allah, the Exalted, said: 'Is He who is standing over every soul (Nafs) by what it has earned?' And Allah, the Exalted, said: 'Does he not know that Allah sees?' And Allah, the Exalted, said: 'Indeed, Allah has ever been, over you, a vigilant watcher (Raqib).' And Allah, the Exalted, said: 'And those who are to their trusts and their covenant caretakers (Ra'un), and those who are to their testimonies standing (Qa'imun).'", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monitoring and Accounting", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Monitoring and Accounting'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "الحمد لله القائم على كل نفس بما كسبت الرقيب على كل جارحة بما اجترحت المطلع على ضمائر القلوب إذا هجست الحسيب على خواطر عباده إذا اختلجت الذى لا يعزب عن علمه مثقال ذرة في السموات والأرض تحركت أو سكنت المحاسب على النقير والقطمير والقليل والكثير من الأعمال وإن خفيت المتفضل بقبول طاعات العباد وان صغرت المتطول بالعفو عن من معاصيهم وإن كثرت وإنما يحاسبهم لتعلم كل نفس ما أحضرت وتنظر فيما قدمت وأخرت فتعلم انه لولا لزومها للمراقبة والمحاسبة في الدنيا لشفيت في صعيد القيامة وهلكت وبعد المجاهدة والمحاسبة وال", "english": "Praise be to Allah, The One Who Stands (Qā'im) over every soul (Nafs) with what it has earned, The Watcher (Raqīb) over every limb with what it has committed, The One Who Sees (Muṭṭaliʿ) into the secrets of the hearts (Qulūb) when they whisper, The Reckoner (Ḥasīb) over the thoughts of His servants when they stir, He from Whose knowledge does not escape the weight of an atom in the heavens and the earth whether it moves or rests, The Accountant (Muḥāsib) over the smallest speck (Naqīr) and the tiniest particle (Qaṭmīr) and the little and the much of deeds even if hidden, The Bestower of Favor (Mutaḍaḍḍil) by accepting the obediences of the servants even if small, The One Who Extends (Mutaṭawwil) with forgiveness for their sins even if many. And He only accounts them so that every soul (Nafs) may know what it has brought forth and look into what it has sent ahead and left behind, so it knows that were it not for its adherence to vigilance (Murāqabah) and self-accounting (Muḥāsabah) in this world, it would be exposed on the plain of the Resurrection and perish. And after striving (Mujāhadah) and self-accounting (Muḥāsabah) and vigilance (Murāqabah), were it not for His favor in accepting its paltry merchandise, it would fail and lose. So glory be to Him Whose blessing has encompassed all the servants and Whose mercy has enveloped and overwhelmed the creatures in this world and the Hereafter and flooded. And by the breaths of His favor, the hearts (Qulūb) expanded for faith (Īmān) and opened up, and by the blessing of His enabling (Tawfīq), the limbs became bound to acts of worship and disciplined, and by the goodness of His guidance (Hidāyah), the darknesses of ignorance (Jahl) cleared from the hearts (Qulūb) and dispersed, and by His support (Taʾyīd) and victory (Nuṣrah), the schemes of Satan (Shayṭān) were cut off and repelled, and by the gentleness of His care (ʿInāyah), the scale of good deeds (Ḥasanāt) tips when it becomes heavy, and by His facilitation (Taysīr), what has been facilitated of obediences (Ṭāʿāt) is facilitated. So from Him is the giving and the recompense, the distancing and the bringing near, the making happy and the making wretched. And prayers and peace be upon Muhammad, the master of the prophets, and upon.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monitoring and Accounting", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monitoring and Accounting'", "badge": "Insight"}], "34": [{"arabic": "فمنها الحسد، وقد قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم: ((الحسد يأكل الحسنات كما تأكل النار الحطب))[119]. ولا ينفك المناظر عن الحسد فإنه تارة يغلب وتارة يغلب وتارة يحمد كلامه وأخرى يحمد كلام غيره فما دام يبقى في الدنيا واحد يذكره بقوة العلم والنظر أو يظن أنه أحسن منه كلاما وأقوى نظرا فلا بد أن يحسده ويحب زوال النعم عنه وانصراف القلوب والوجوه عنه إليه والحسد نار محرقة فمن بلى به فهو في العذاب في الدنيا ولعذاب الآخرة أشد وأعظم ولذلك قال ابن عباس رضي الله عنهما خذوا العلم حيث وجدتموه ولا تقبلوا قول الفق", "english": "From them is envy (Hasad), and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'Envy (Hasad) consumes good deeds as fire consumes firewood.' And the disputant is not free from envy (Hasad), for sometimes he prevails and sometimes he is prevailed over, sometimes his speech is praised and other times the speech of another is praised. As long as there remains in the world one who is mentioned with strength of knowledge (Ilm) and consideration (Nadhar) or it is thought that he has better speech and stronger consideration (Nadhar) than him, it is inevitable that he envies (Yahsuduhu) him and loves the removal of blessings (Ni'am) from him and the turning of hearts (Qulub) and faces away from him toward himself. And envy (Hasad) is a burning fire, so whoever is afflicted with it is in punishment (Adhab) in the worldly life (Al-Hayat Al-Dunya), and the punishment (Adhab) of the Hereafter (Al-Akhirah) is more severe and greater. And therefore Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: 'Take knowledge (Ilm) wherever you find it, and do not accept the saying of the jurists (Fuqaha) about each other, for they become envious (Yataghayyarun) as goats become envious (Tataghayyar) in the pen.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "37": [{"arabic": "ه فذكر كل واحد منهم ما رآه غالباً على نفسه أو على من كان يخاطبه، فقال بشر رحمه الله تعالى: الزهد في الدنيا هو الزهد في الناس، وهذا إشارة إلى الزهد في الجاه خاصة. وقال قاسم الجوعي: الزهد في الدنيا هو الزهد في الجوف، فبقدر ما تملك من بطنك كذلك تملك من الزهد، وهذا إشارة إلى الزهد في شهوة واحدة، ولعمري هي أغلب الشهرات على الأكثر وهي المهيجة لأكثر الشهوات. وقال الفضيل: الزهد في الدنيا هو القناعة، وهذا إشارة إلى المال خاصة. وقال الثوري: الزهد هو قصر الأمل، وهو جامع لجميع الشهوات، فإن من يميل إلى الشهو", "english": "Then each one mentioned what he saw as predominant upon himself or upon whom he was addressing, so Bishr, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: Asceticism (Zuhd) in the world is asceticism (Zuhd) in people, and this is an indication to asceticism (Zuhd) in status (Jah) specifically. And Qasim al-Ju'i said: Asceticism (Zuhd) in the world is asceticism (Zuhd) in the belly (Jawf), so according to what you possess from your stomach, thus you possess from asceticism (Zuhd), and this is an indication to asceticism (Zuhd) in one desire (Shahwah), and by my life, it is the most prevalent of the desires (Shahwat) for the majority and it is the inciter for most desires (Shahwat). And al-Fudayl said: Asceticism (Zuhd) in the world is contentment (Qana'ah), and this is an indication to wealth specifically. And al-Thawri said: Asceticism (Zuhd) is shortening hope (Qasr al-Amal), and it is comprehensive of all desires (Shahwat), for indeed whoever inclines to desires (Shahwat), then whoever inclines to desires (Shahwat) tells himself of permanence, so his hope (Amal) lengthens, and whoever shortens his hope (Amal) is as if he has turned away from all desires (Shahwat). And Uways said: If the ascetic (Zahid) goes out seeking, asceticism (Zuhd) departs from him, and he did not intend by this but made reliance (Tawakkul) a condition in asceticism (Zuhd). And Uways also said: Asceticism (Zuhd) is abandoning seeking for what is guaranteed (Mudman), and it is an indication to provision (Rizq). And the people of hadith said: Love of the world is acting by opinion (Ra'y) and reason (Ma'qul), and asceticism (Zuhd) is indeed following knowledge ('Ilm) and adhering to the Sunnah, and this if what is intended is corrupt opinion (Ra'y) and reason (Ma'qul) by which status (Jah) in the world is sought, then it is correct, but it is an indication to some of what is from superfluous desires (Shahwat), for indeed from the sciences ('Ulum) is what has no benefit in the Hereafter, and they have prolonged them until the lifespan of the human is spent in occupation with one of them, so the condition of the ascetic (Zahid) is that superfluities (Fudul) are the first thing repelled from him, and al-Hasan said: The ascetic (Zahid) when he sees someone says: This is better than me, so he went to that asceticism (Zuhd) is humility (Tawadu'), and this is an indication to negating status (Jah) and pride ('Ujb) and it is some of the divisions of asceticism (Zuhd). And some of them said: Asceticism (Zuhd) is seeking the lawful (Halal), and where is this from one who says: Asceticism (Zuhd) is abandoning seeking as Uways said, and there is no doubt that he intended by it abandoning seeking the lawful (Halal) and indeed Yusuf ibn Asbat used to say: Whoever is patient upon harm and abandons desires (Shahwat) and eats bread from the lawful (Halal) has taken the foundation of asceticism (Zuhd). And in asceticism (Zuhd) there are sayings beyond what we have transmitted, so we did not see benefit in transmitting them, for indeed whoever seeks to uncover the realities (Haqa'iq) of matters from the sayings of people sees them differing, so he does not benefit except confusion, and as for whoever the truth (Haqq) is unveiled to him in himself and he attains it by witnessing (Mushahadah) from his heart (Qalb) not by catching from his hearing, then he has trusted in the truth (Haqq) and observed the deficiency of whoever is deficient due to deficiency in his insight (Basirah), and the limitation of whoever limited with complete knowledge (Ma'rifah) due to limitation of his need, and these all limited not due to deficiency in insight (Basirah) but they mentioned what they mentioned at the time of need, so no wonder they mentioned it according to the need, and needs differ so no wonder the words differ, and the cause of limitation may be informing about the...", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}], "38": [{"arabic": "وقال تعالى في وصف الرسل ومدحهم (ولقد أرسلنا رسلا من قبلك وجعلنا لهم أزواجا وذرية) فذكر ذلك في معرض الامتنان وإظهار الفضل ومدح أولياءه بسؤال ذلك في الدعاء فقال (والذين يقولون ربنا هب لنا من أزواجنا وذرياتنا قرة أعين) الآية ويقال إن الله تعالى لم يذكر في كتابه من الأنبياء إلا المتأهلين فقالوا إن يحيى صلى الله عليه وسلم قد تزوج ولم يجامع قيل إنما فعل ذلك لنيل الفضل وإقامة السنة وقيل لغض البصر وأما عيسى عليه السلام فإنه سينكح إذا نزل الأرض ويولد له.", "english": "And He, the Exalted, said in describing the Messengers and praising them: 'And We have certainly sent messengers before you and made for them wives and offspring' (Quran 13:38). He mentioned that in the context of showing favor and manifesting excellence, and praising His allies by requesting that in supplication, as He said: 'And those who say: Our Lord, grant us from our wives and our offspring comfort of the eyes' (Quran 25:74) the verse. And it is said that Allah, the Exalted, did not mention in His Book from the Prophets except those who were married. They said that Yahya (John), peace be upon him, married but did not have intercourse; it is said he did that only to attain excellence and establish the Sunnah (Prophetic tradition), and it is said for lowering the gaze. As for Isa (Jesus), peace be upon him, he will marry when he descends to the earth and children will be born to him.", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k02.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Marriage", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance, from 'Etiquette of Marriage'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "43": [{"arabic": "وقال تعالى: ﴿قل كفى بالله شهيدا بيني وبينكم ومن عنده علم الكتاب﴾ وقال تعالى: ﴿قال الذي عنده علم من الكتاب أنا آتيك به﴾ تنبيها على أنه اقتدر بقوة العلم.", "english": "And He (Allah) the Exalted said: 'Say: Sufficient is Allah as a witness between me and you, and whoever has knowledge (ilm) of the Book.' And He (Allah) the Exalted said: 'Said the one who had knowledge (ilm) from the Book: I will bring it to you' - pointing out that he was empowered by the strength of knowledge (ilm).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Afterlife"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 3057], [2, 3057, 4079], [3, 4079, 6055], [4, 6055, 7724], [5, 7724, 10637], [6, 10637, 12068], [7, 12068, 13669], [8, 13669, 14350], [9, 14350, 15883], [10, 15883, 17416]